Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Insufficient Disk Space
Problem: Cloning fails due to insufficient disk space.

Solution:

# Check available disk space
df -h /var/lib/libvirt/images/

# Clean up old VM images if needed
sudo virsh vol-list default
sudo virsh vol-delete --pool default old-vm.qcow2

# Use linked clones to save space
sudo /opt/vm-automation/clone-vm.sh template-vm space-saver linked
Issue 2: Network Conflicts
Problem: Cloned VMs have duplicate MAC addresses or IP conflicts.

Solution:

# Remove MAC address from VM definition to auto-generate new one
sudo virsh edit problematic-vm
# Delete the <mac address='...' /> line

# Restart VM to get new MAC
sudo virsh destroy problematic-vm
sudo virsh start problematic-vm

# Check new MAC address
sudo virsh dumpxml problematic-vm | grep "mac address"
Issue 3: Cloud-init Not Working
Problem: Cloud-init configuration not being applied to cloned VMs.

Solution:

# Verify cloud-init ISO is attached
sudo virsh dumpxml vm-name | grep -A5 cdrom

# Check cloud-init logs inside VM
sudo virsh console vm-name
# Inside VM: sudo journalctl -u cloud-init

# Recreate cloud-init ISO with correct format
sudo genisoimage -output /var/lib/libvirt/images/vm-cloud-init.iso \
    -volid cidata -joliet -rock user-data meta-data
Issue 4: Performance Issues with Linked Clones
Problem: Linked clones showing poor performance.

Solution:

# Check backing file chain depth
sudo qemu-img info --backing-chain /var/lib/libvirt/images/linked-vm.qcow2

# Commit changes to reduce chain depth if needed
sudo qemu-img commit /var/lib/libvirt/images/linked-vm.qcow2

# Consider converting to full clone for production use
sudo qemu-img convert -O qcow2 linked-vm.qcow2 full-vm.qcow2
